  "headline": "Polda NTT Questions Witnesses in Alleged Kupang Regent Rape Case",
  "seoTitle": "Polda NTT Questions Witnesses in Kupang Regent Rape Probe",
  "metaDescription": "Police in East Nusa Tenggara are questioning witnesses and have received Ministry of Home Affairs approval to investigate Kupang Regent Yosef Lede.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Investigators from the NTT Regional Police have questioned over a dozen witnesses regarding allegations of sexual violence involving Kupang Regent Yosef Lede.",
    "The Ministry of Home Affairs has formally granted permission for authorities to proceed with the examination and potential detention of the official.",
    "Police previously conducted a search of the regent's official residence and the home of a witness, securing several items of evidence for analysis."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The investigation into allegations of sexual assault involving Kupang Regent Yosef Lede has intensified as NTT regional authorities move forward with legal proceedings. Police have officially initiated a notification of commencement of investigation and issued investigation warrants. Authorities have conducted multiple searches, including at the regent's official residence and the home of an individual identified as EK, where various items were seized as evidence. The Ministry of Home Affairs has issued the necessary permits to allow investigators to examine and detain the official if required. Recent developments also include the questioning of the alleged victim and over a dozen additional witnesses. Amidst the ongoing probe, the Director of the Women and Children Protection Unit at the NTT Regional Police has been reassigned. Officials have addressed public concerns regarding the status of the case, emphasizing the ongoing nature of the evidence review.",
